    {
      "text": "6. Conclusions",
      "bbox": [
        287.0140075683594,
        445.26397705078125,
        361.7014465332031,
        454.1107482910156
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Robust Bayesian analysis (i.e. Bayesian inference under a set of priors) oﬀers a way to quantify",
      "bbox": [
        122.11601257324219,
        463.1969909667969,
        538.5925903320312,
        472.04376220703125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "epistemic uncertainty by bounded instead of precise probability. This type of analysis is useful for",
      "bbox": [
        110.1610107421875,
        475.1519775390625,
        538.6323852539062,
        483.9987487792969
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "evaluating sensitivity to the choice of prior. It is also a solution for Bayesian inference when prior",
      "bbox": [
        110.1610107421875,
        487.1069641113281,
        538.6124267578125,
        495.9537353515625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "information is upfront given as a set of distributions.",
      "bbox": [
        110.1610107421875,
        499.0629577636719,
        340.8250427246094,
        507.90972900390625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "We have derived an expression for the eﬀective sample size of importance sampling with corre-",
      "bbox": [
        122.11601257324219,
        511.0179748535156,
        538.562744140625,
        519.86474609375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "lated MCMC samples, which ensures reliable samples from both MCMC and importance sampling",
      "bbox": [
        110.1610107421875,
        522.972900390625,
        538.5826416015625,
        531.8197021484375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "procedures when combining them. The combination of iterative importance sampling with MCMC",
      "bbox": [
        110.1610107421875,
        534.9279174804688,
        538.6026611328125,
        543.7747192382812
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "sampling was used for robust Bayesian analysis on an existing meta-analysis based on a random",
      "bbox": [
        110.1610107421875,
        546.8829345703125,
        538.5824584960938,
        555.729736328125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "eﬀects model [4]. The estimated lower bound on the expected overall eﬀect of the intervention in",
      "bbox": [
        110.1610107421875,
        558.837890625,
        538.5728149414062,
        567.6846923828125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "the meta-analysis is a conservative estimate compared to what would have been the result from",
      "bbox": [
        110.1610107421875,
        570.7938842773438,
        538.5628662109375,
        579.6406860351562
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "selecting one prior in the set and using a standard Bayesian analysis.",
      "bbox": [
        110.1610107421875,
        582.7489013671875,
        411.6192626953125,
        591.595703125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Iterative importance sampling with MCMC sampling allows for robust Bayesian analysis on a",
      "bbox": [
